[0.011, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Why did enterprise signups fall 3% in the week of 22 May 2026?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 91s over 6 steps, 24,852 tokens, 17 observations gathered, 12 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The available data cannot confirm that enterprise signups fell 3% in the week of 22 May 2026: the only signup series accessible is an unsegmented, all-plan total that shows no fall in that week, and two separate attempts to break it down by plan or URL both returned the same unsegmented figures rather than an enterprise-specific view.  [posthog.event_trend e7703522, posthog.event_trend 3b601160]\r\n  GA4 sessions actually rose during the week of 22 May compared to the prior week, giving no supporting signal of a broader traffic or funnel decline.  [ga4.get_sessions e8409164]\r\n  HubSpot CRM data, GitHub co"]
[0.000, "o", "mmit history, and Slack search all returned empty for this window, so no deploy, CRM, or internal-discussion evidence could be found to test candidate causes.  [hubspot.contacts 820b94d7, hubspot.search e28842e7, hubspot.closed_won f09b0597, github.commits d8044a84, github.commits 730b577b, slack.search_messages f32e6932, slack.search_messages 9068743f, slack.find_decision 501d200c]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  No enterprise-segmented signup data exists for the window  (high)\r\n    - The event trend for 'user signed up' from 15–28 May 2026 returns only an aggregate count of all signups; requesting a breakdown by 'plan' or by '$current_url' returned identical unsegmented totals, indicating no plan/segment dimension was actually applied.  [posthog.event_trend e7703522, posthog.event_trend 3b601160]\r\n    - Total signups over the two weeks range from 25 to 28 per day with no visible break around 22 May, the date the question identifies as the star"]
[0.000, "o", "t of the fall.  [posthog.event_trend e7703522]\r\n    - HubSpot contains no contact or deal records at all for 15–28 May 2026, so enterprise signups (which would typically be tracked as HubSpot leads/deals) cannot be measured from CRM data for this window either.  [hubspot.contacts 820b94d7, hubspot.search e28842e7, hubspot.closed_won f09b0597]\r\n  No corroborating signal of a fall in any adjacent metric  (medium)\r\n    - GA4 daily sessions for 15–28 May 2026 actually rose across the week of 22 May (708, 690, 710, 704, 715, 689, 648) compared to the prior week (685, 659, 676, 666, 663, 682, 682), showing no decline in top-of-funnel traffic that would explain a signup drop.  [ga4.get_sessions e8409164]\r\n    - A GA4 channel-level comparison between the two weeks returned zero rows, so no channel-level breakdown is available to support or contradict a change in acquisition mix.  [ga4.compare_periods 0861f369]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  user signed"]
[0.000, "o", " up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |█▃██▆██▁█▆▃▁█▆|  25 → 28\r\n                        2026-05-15 … 2026-05-28\r\n\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |█▃██▆██▁█▆▃▁█▆|  25 → 28\r\n                        2026-05-15 … 2026-05-28\r\n\r\n  sessions over time\r\n  sessions\r\n    sessions           |▅▂▄▃▃▅▅▇▅▇▇█▅▁|  648 → 715\r\n                        2026-05-15 … 2026-05-28\r\n\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] A product deploy to acme/product or acme/web caused a drop in enterprise signups around 22 May 2026.\r\n      No commits were found in either repository for the window, which would rule this out, but commit history returning empty is also consistent with the connector not covering this period, so this is treated as inconclusive rather than contradicted.\r\n  [inconclusive] A sales/marketing or CRM-side change r"]
[0.000, "o", "educed enterprise lead flow, visible as a drop in HubSpot deals or contacts.\r\n      HubSpot returned zero contacts and zero deals for the entire window, both before and after 22 May, which cannot distinguish a decline from a total absence of connected data for this period.\r\n  [contradicted] The premise that enterprise signups fell 3% in the week of 22 May is correct and measurable in the available data.\r\n      The only signup series available is not segmented by enterprise vs. other plans despite two different breakdown attempts, and the aggregate series shows no fall of that magnitude beginning 22 May — daily totals stayed in a tight 25-28 band throughout.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P1 Confirm with the data/analytics team whether PostHog events carry a plan or segment property that identifies 'enterprise' users, and re-run the breakdown using the correct property name before re-investigating this question.\r\n      why: Both breakdown"]
[0.001, "o", " attempts ('plan', '$current_url') returned unsegmented totals identical to the unfiltered trend, indicating the property name used does not exist or does not distinguish enterprise accounts — the current data cannot support or refute the original claim.\r\n      [posthog.event_trend e7703522, posthog.event_trend 3b601160]\r\n  P1 Verify HubSpot connector coverage for May 2026 by checking a known-active period, since zero contacts and zero deals were returned for the entire 15–28 May window.\r\n      why: A complete absence of CRM records for two weeks is itself unusual and should be checked as a possible data gap rather than accepted as an accurate picture of enterprise pipeline activity.\r\n      [hubspot.contacts 820b94d7, hubspot.search e28842e7, hubspot.closed_won f09b0597]\r\n  P2 Ask whoever raised the original 3% figure which system and definition produced it, so the correct source can be queried directly.\r\n      why: None of the connected sources (PostHog aggregate, GA4, HubSpot) reproduce a 3% enterprise-"]
[0.000, "o", "specific weekly decline, so the number likely originates from a report or dashboard outside the tools available here.\r\n      [posthog.event_trend e7703522, ga4.get_sessions e8409164]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The 'enterprise' segment cannot be isolated in PostHog (no working plan/segment breakdown was returned), so a real enterprise-specific decline could be masked within a flat all-plan total.\r\n  - HubSpot returning zero rows for the entire two-week window for both contacts and deals suggests either a connector gap or a lifecycle-stage/date filter mismatch, not necessarily zero real activity — this should be verified before concluding CRM was quiet.\r\n  - GitHub commit history was empty for both acme/product and acme/web across the full window, which is unusual for active repositories and suggests the connector may not be returning commits for this period rather than there being no deploys.\r\n  - 1 claim(s) were removed because a"]
[0.000, "o", "n independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - 1 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- findings[1].claims[0]: The evidence exactly matches the numbers cited and shows the second week's values generally higher than the first week's, supporting the traffic comparison, though the causal infer\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - PostHog breakdown_property requests for 'plan' and '$current_url' both returned results identical to the unfiltered total series, suggesting the breakdown was not actually applied or the property does not exist in this dataset.\r\n  - HubSpot contacts, deals search, and closed-won queries all returned zero rows for the full 15–28 May window, which may reflect a connector or filter issue rather than genuine zero activity.\r\n  "]
[0.000, "o", "- GitHub commit history was empty for acme/product and acme/web for the full window despite both being active, non-archived repositories, suggesting the commits endpoint may not cover this date range.\r\n  - GA4 channel comparison between the two weeks returned zero comparison rows despite the underlying sessions series having data, indicating the comparison query itself did not resolve.\r\n  - 9 of the 12 cited observation(s) returned no results (ga4.compare_periods, github.commits, hubspot.closed_won, hubspot.contacts, hubspot.search, slack.find_decision, slack.search_messages). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  0861f369  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  e8409164  ga4.get_sessions  eval://ga4__get_sessions\r\n  d8044a84  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  730b577b  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  f09b0597  hubspot.clo"]
